"""Original self-service and workflow administration cases."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(o,rows):
 for k,(s,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((s,[o[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(o) if j!=k],e))
group(['Review knowledge read criteria','Review knowledge contribute criteria','Inspect article publication state','Run user-criteria diagnostics'],[
('An approved audience needs to read a knowledge base but does not need to author or retire its articles. Which access configuration directly addresses that requirement?', 'Read criteria determine the permitted readership; contribution is a separate, broader capability.'),
('A designated editorial team needs to create and maintain articles in a knowledge base. Which access configuration should be evaluated?', 'Contribute criteria govern the relevant authoring and maintenance access, subject to additional article and ownership controls.'),
('An intended reader meets the knowledge access criteria, but the new article is still being authored and has not been released. Which lifecycle detail should be checked?', 'Publication state matters independently of audience access. A draft is not made published merely by granting read criteria.'),
('An administrator needs evidence of which criteria match a particular user and explain that user’s knowledge access. Which diagnostic capability fits?', 'User-criteria diagnostics evaluates the selected user’s criteria-based access rather than guessing from the user’s job title.')])
group(['Draft','Review','Published','Pending retirement'],[
('An author is creating a new version of a knowledge article and has not submitted it for approval. Which state fits this work?', 'Draft represents the version being created or revised before review.'),
('A draft knowledge version has been sent to designated reviewers to approve or reject. Which state describes that stage?', 'Review indicates that the draft version is awaiting the review decision.'),
('A knowledge article has completed its required approval and has been released for its permitted audience. Which state describes that version?', 'Published indicates the approved, published version; audience access still applies.'),
('An existing published article has been selected for withdrawal, but the required retirement approval has not yet completed. Which state fits?', 'Pending retirement distinguishes the approval stage from completed retirement.')])
group(['A standard catalog item','A record producer','An order guide','A reusable variable set'],[
('Employees need to request a particular accessory through the normal requested-item fulfillment process. Which catalog building block fits?', 'A standard catalog item supports the normal item request and fulfillment process.'),
('A team wants a simplified self-service intake that creates a task-based record directly, rather than a requested item. Which catalog building block fits?', 'A record producer creates the task-based record through catalog-style intake; it should not be used to bypass normal requested-item creation.'),
('A new employee request should guide the requester through several related catalog items in one coordinated experience. Which building block fits?', 'An order guide brings related items together for a defined purpose.'),
('Several catalog items ask the same maintained set of location and contact questions. The team wants to reuse that question group. Which building block fits?', 'A variable set packages related variables for reuse across catalog items or order guides.')])
group(['Apply criteria to the individual item','Inspect Not Available For matches','Use a second category association','Review access outside the catalog'],[
('A category is restricted, but an item also appears through another permitted catalog path. The item itself must be restricted to the intended audience. Which configuration should be added?', 'Category restrictions do not automatically become restrictions on each item. Apply the appropriate criteria to the item itself.'),
('A user matches an item’s Available For criteria but still cannot access it. The same user also matches an exclusion criterion. Which setting explains the denial?', 'Not Available For overrides Available For for the item; the exclusion must be evaluated.'),
('A service should be discoverable under both Facilities and Workplace without maintaining two independent copies of the item. Which catalog organization change fits?', 'An item can belong to multiple categories, supporting multiple discovery paths without duplicating its definition.'),
('An item is hidden by catalog user criteria, but an authorized user can still access its table record outside Service Catalog. Which distinction should the administrator evaluate?', 'Catalog criteria apply within the catalog context. Separate table access controls govern access outside that context.')])
group(['A record-created trigger','A record-updated trigger','A scheduled trigger','A Service Catalog trigger'],[
('A flow should start when a new qualifying record is inserted into a supported custom non-system table. Which trigger category fits?', 'A record-created trigger starts from creation of a record on the selected supported table.'),
('A flow should respond when an existing qualifying record on a supported table changes, with the run condition explicitly configured. Which trigger category fits?', 'A record-updated trigger addresses changes to existing records and needs the appropriate run conditions.'),
('A maintenance flow should begin on a defined weekly schedule rather than depend on a particular record being changed. Which trigger category fits?', 'A scheduled trigger starts based on time rather than a record operation.'),
('A flow is intended to fulfill a requested catalog item using the dedicated request mechanism. Which trigger category fits?', 'The Service Catalog trigger starts the associated fulfillment flow from a catalog item request.')])
group(['Extract a reusable subflow','Supply the subflow inputs','Use the returned subflow outputs','Test the subflow in isolation'],[
('Several flows repeat the same sequence of business operations. The administrator wants one maintained sequence callable by all of them. Which change fits?', 'A subflow provides reusable operations that multiple flows can call.'),
('A reusable subflow needs a particular record and a requested date for each invocation. Which caller responsibility supplies those changing values?', 'The caller maps the required inputs for that invocation; a subflow does not obtain them from its own record trigger.'),
('A subflow returns an approved routing result that a later caller step needs. Which part of the interface should the caller consume?', 'Defined outputs communicate results back to the caller for subsequent steps.'),
('A reusable subflow behaves unexpectedly and the designer wants to exercise it with controlled example inputs on a test instance. Which validation action fits?', 'Test the subflow independently with defined inputs. Testing can change records, so use suitable non-production data.')])
group(['Define the decision inputs','Add the decision rows','Inspect the result columns','Test representative input combinations'],[
('A routing decision needs to consider country and request category, but those values are not yet represented in its interface. Which design step is missing?', 'Decision inputs provide the values used to evaluate the decision logic.'),
('The decision table has its inputs and result structure, but no entries connecting condition values to outcomes. Which content must be added?', 'Decision rows express the configured combinations and their results.'),
('A decision correctly matches the intended row but returns the wrong routing field. Which part of the decision structure should be reviewed?', 'Result columns describe the values returned for the matched decision outcome.'),
('A decision table has been saved and the owner wants to confirm its outcomes for normal, boundary and exceptional cases. Which action fits?', 'Test representative input combinations against expected outcomes before relying on the decision in a process.')])
group(['Publish the completed topic','Reuse a topic block','Review the topic’s application scope','Test the conversation path'],[
('A Virtual Agent topic is complete but remains inactive and has not been deployed to clients. Which lifecycle action makes the finished topic active?', 'Publishing changes the completed topic from inactive to active and deploys it to clients under the supported process.'),
('Several Virtual Agent conversations need the same common sequence of conversational tasks. Which design change reduces duplicated maintenance?', 'A reusable topic block supplies common conversational functionality to calling topics.'),
('A designer is about to create a topic intended for a particular application but the current application context is different. Which check should occur first?', 'Confirm the appropriate application scope before creating or changing the topic.'),
('A topic has a branch that has never been exercised with realistic user answers. Which activity checks whether that branch reaches its intended outcome?', 'Test the conversation path using representative responses rather than treating publication alone as validation.')])
group(['Inspect the trigger conditions','Inspect the runtime input values','Inspect the failing action details','Inspect the reporting configuration'],[
('A new qualifying record never starts the expected flow, and the configured trigger excludes its category. Which area explains the missing execution?', 'The trigger conditions determine whether an execution starts. Downstream action changes cannot correct an excluded trigger population.'),
('A tested flow runs, but the recipient passed to an action differs from the requester on the record. Which evidence directly helps trace the mapping?', 'Runtime input values show what the action actually received, helping distinguish a mapping error from its intended design.'),
('A test execution stops at one action while earlier steps complete. Which evidence should be examined to understand the local failure?', 'The failing action’s execution details provide relevant state, inputs and error context when generated and accessible.'),
('A historical production run has no detailed action values because detailed reporting was off at the time. Which configuration explains the missing detail?', 'Execution detail generation depends on the reporting configuration. Enabling it later cannot recreate values that were never recorded.')])
group(['Validate the requested-item path','Check the knowledge audience','Check the reusable component contract','Check the automation’s actual result'],[
('A catalog implementation creates an incident when the requirement calls for a requested item with standard fulfillment. Which design mismatch should be corrected?', 'Validate the standard requested-item path and appropriate catalog item mechanism rather than using direct task production for a different purpose.'),
('A help article is correctly published but contains guidance intended only for a restricted internal team. Which release check is still necessary?', 'Verify the permitted knowledge audience; publication state and audience authorization solve different problems.'),
('A shared subflow changes the name and meaning of an output consumed by several callers. Which compatibility review is needed?', 'Review the component interface and affected callers so the changed output does not break their assumptions.'),
('An automation execution reports completion, but its business owner has not checked the created records or assignments. Which final validation is needed?', 'Confirm the actual business result against the requirement. Technical completion alone does not prove that the configured process produced the correct outcome.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==40
